{{also|eloqüent|éloquent}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|eloquent}}, from {{der|en|la|eloquens||speaking, having the faculty of speech, eloquent}}, present participle of {{m|la|eloqui||to speak out}}, from {{m|la|e||out}} + {{m|la|loqui||to speak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛl.əˌkwənt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-eloquent.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[fluently|Fluently]] [[persuasive]] and [[articulate]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''eloquent''' writer}}
# [[effective|Effective]] in [[expressing]] [[meaning]] by [[speech]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''eloquent''' article}}

====Usage notes====
''Eloquent'' expresses stronger praise than do {{m|en|articulate}} or {{m|en|well-spoken}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|articulate}}
* {{l|en|well-spoken}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|eloquate}}
* {{l|en|eloquently}}

